  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b4d3-97c3-a3df-6960" name="Achaemenid Persian (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ACHAEMENID PERSIAN ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.12-13), 550-330 BC.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Persian Troops up to three quarters of the points; Levies &amp; Mercenaries at least a quarter; Special Troops up to a quarter, with at most one bolt thrower or war wagon per 500 points and one elephant per 1,000 points.
Spara: infantry may carry large shields (spara) that count as shields unless set up as a barrier (hard cover to the front against missiles, defended obstacle in combat; knocked down if the unit moves or loses a round).

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Persian Troops: up to 75%
  Levies &amp; Mercenaries: at least 25%
  Special Troops: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
